From: Muhammad Huda Nugroho <mhudan21@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] daemon: persist v6state across the context rebuild

Patch 1/2 keeps the "IPv6 unavailable" decision on a per-interface object
(v6state) rather than in the context's `self`, because a modem that crashes on
a refused-v6 teardown makes the daemon rebuild the context - which would reset
any state held in `self` and re-arm the crash loop.

Carry v6state across the rebuild the same way `_failed_at` and
`reconnect_on_register` are carried (from the previous entry via `prev`), and
hand the live object to the context factory so the context reads and updates it
in place. A fresh interface starts with an empty {} (v6 attempted normally).

Signed-off-by: Muhammad Huda Nugroho <mhudan21@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src-ucode/daemon.uc
+++ b/src-ucode/daemon.uc
@@ -3159,6 +3159,9 @@
 		             // entry can fail to exist across a reload, and then there
 		             // is nothing to carry it from.)
 		             _failed_at: prev?._failed_at,
+		             // IPv6-unavailable state (context.uc v6state) — carried so
+		             // it survives the modem-crash-driven context rebuild.
+		             v6state: prev?.v6state ?? {},
 		             // ...or, after a daemon restart, from the file
 		             reconnect_on_register: prev?.reconnect_on_register ?? restored };

@@ -3177,6 +3180,7 @@
 			name: name,
 			modem: mentry.modem,
 			config: cfg,
+			v6state: entry.v6state,
 			timing: opts?.ctx_timing,
 			deps: {
 				log: (level, msg) => log(level, sprintf('interface %s: %s', name, msg)),
